      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "even if you've read the documents, it can be strange.\nI've found I have better results with the calibration if I do a Real-Life T-pose while looking straight forward before pressing both triggers.  I don't know if this is a bug, or a nuance of my trackers, or \"working as intended, suggested by the devs\" but it doesn't appear in the documents from what I've seen.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
